{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]I had a friend named Ramblin' Bob
[C]Who used to steal, gamble and rob
[C]He thought he was the smartest guy in [F]town
[F]But I found out last Monday, that Bob got locked up Sunday
They’ve [D]got him in the jailhouse way [G]downtown
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]He's in the jailhouse [C]now
[C]He's in the jailhouse [F]now
I [G]told him once or twice
[G]To quit playin' cards and shootin' dice
[G]He's in the jailhouse [C]now
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Oh lay-eee, [F]Ee-ee-ee-heee
Oh de oh, [C]Ee-ee-ee-heee
Ah-eee-oh, [G]lay-ee-heee, yee-de-la-hee
[C]Oh-lay-heeee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
He played a game called poker
Pee-knuckle, whist and Yoh-ker
But shootin’ dice was his greatest game
Now he’s downtown in jail, nobody to go his bail
The judge done said that he refused a fine
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
I went out last Tuesday
Met a girl named Susie
I told her I was the swellest man around
We started t’ spend my money
Then she started to call me honey
We took in every cabaret in town
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
Chorus & Yodel
{end_of_verse}
